Qstn ) : You are given a large number (of type long long) and another integer. Your task is to divide the large number with the integer and print the result with exactly 2 decimal place.
Ans ) : (in C++)
#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;
long division(int num, int divisor){
    double result;
    result = double(num)/divisor ;
    cout<< fixed << setprecision (2) << result << endl;
    return 0;
}

int main() {
    // Write Your Code here...
    int num;
    int divisor;
    cin >> num >> divisor ;
    division(num,divisor);
    return 0;
}
Problems : if you take result as double only then it will work otherwise it will do the integer division first. I took long at first but got the issue because the issue is that long is still an integer type, not a floating-point type.
